FIXED: Superfluous port names in a `Synthesize` annotation are no longer silently ignored. Listing more `PortName`s than there are ports (either at the top level of `t_inputs`, or inside a `PortProduct`) now raises an error instead of dropping the extra names. This used to be especially confusing when removing an argument shifted all subsequent port names onto the wrong ports. See [#2243](https://github.com/clash-lang/clash-compiler/issues/2243).
